    "q-101299": {
      "dom_id": "step-q101299",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If ${a}_{n+1}=7{a}_{n}-3$ with ${a}_{1}=1,$ then ${a}_{3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=7{a}_{n}-3.\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}=1.$\n\nWe use this formula to compute the terms ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}$ as follows:\n\n- We first compute ${a}_{2}$ by substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & =7{a}_{n}-3 \\\\ {a}_{1+1} & =7{a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =7{a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =7(1)-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${a}_{3}$ by substituting $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & =7{a}_{n}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2+1} & =7{a}_{2}-3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =7{a}_{2}-3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =7(4)-3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{3}=25.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
